+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis holds on each interval where $\\operatorname{sin}(x - 3)\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694030 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2922c9f0-92c7-54aa-b1bc-8713a4829bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694028} {:answer/id #uuid "a91f861e-1477-5655-80de-a9676ba5d8d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694034} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ef433f-84e1-506c-8f77-806feacf3793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694036} {:answer/id #uuid "c7057f1c-d64e-518d-983a-9c268c127450" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1 + \\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694038} {:answer/id #uuid "d5ef222b-dd03-50a1-8c94-937df7b854b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694042}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694036} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e67b05e-d437-52d1-bc23-e904ac4fa5f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4fe76186-1b66-54b0-8bb5-0af3ecb093f6" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} - 2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=- 2 x, & u^\\prime&=-2,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}, & v&=\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[- x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\left(\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\left(-2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[- x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}+\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[- x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)&=- \\frac{\\pi}{4}=- \\frac{\\pi}{4},\\\\\nF\\left(0\\right)&=- \\frac{1}{2}=- \\frac{1}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694031 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28b14a21-47a1-57a4-8efd-8c016017e964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1 - e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694027} {:answer/id #uuid "4a123331-319d-5bf4-9437-1f3e9365759b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1 + e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694029} {:answer/id #uuid "b4a3ce10-ce3f-5369-8c33-2f3e15f51a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1 + 3 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694035} {:answer/id #uuid "c9639572-738f-5a02-9440-796ed8d0e2ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694039} {:answer/id #uuid "e7099de2-3375-5be9-9b3d-c7724a40ee2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694044}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694029} :answer-field/id #uuid "26b13cc2-2281-5a26-bcb5-4e2083e02a44" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694026}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7c3f13b9-9f08-5abf-8bc4-09d3a8f9f34c" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{2} x e^{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=x, & u^\\prime&=1,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=e^{x}, & v&=e^{x}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[x e^{x}\\right]_{0}^{2}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\left(1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[x e^{x}\\right]_{0}^{2}-\\int_{0}^{2}e^{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[x e^{x} - e^{x}\\right]_{0}^{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(2\\right)&=e^{2}=e^{2},\\\\\nF\\left(0\\right)&=-1=-1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(e^{2}\\right)-\\left(-1\\right)\\\\\n&=1 + e^{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694032 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0944a8c-e925-5838-a71e-185be5f7503c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{3} + e^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694041}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694041} :answer-field/id #uuid "f91d6f08-6f6b-5092-908a-ffe4abacac55" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "830106cb-221a-5579-b783-ed41c2699df3" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{2}{3}}^{0} 3 x e^{3 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=3 x, & u^\\prime&=3,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=e^{3 x}, & v&=\\frac{e^{3 x}}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[x e^{3 x}\\right]_{- \\frac{2}{3}}^{0}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{- \\frac{2}{3}}^{0}\\left(\\frac{e^{3 x}}{3}\\right)\\left(3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[x e^{3 x}\\right]_{- \\frac{2}{3}}^{0}-\\int_{- \\frac{2}{3}}^{0}e^{3 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[x e^{3 x} - \\frac{e^{3 x}}{3}\\right]_{- \\frac{2}{3}}^{0}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(0\\right)&=- \\frac{1}{3}=- \\frac{1}{3},\\\\\nF\\left(- \\frac{2}{3}\\right)&=- \\frac{1}{e^{2}}=- \\frac{1}{e^{2}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(- \\frac{1}{3}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{1}{e^{2}}\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\frac{1}{3} + e^{-2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694033 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbace438-7b69-5b06-b987-e0b80fbdb22f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\pi}{9} - \\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694037}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694037} :answer-field/id #uuid "120534b4-87f2-51ea-a712-8c3d27135e88" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9f41da68-af7f-5236-903f-45ebee73bc95" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} 2 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=2 x, & u^\\prime&=2,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}, & v&=\\frac{\\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[\\frac{2 x \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}\\left(\\frac{\\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}\\right)\\left(2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac{2 x \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}\\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[\\frac{2 x \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3} + \\frac{2 \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{9}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)&=- \\frac{2}{9}=- \\frac{2}{9},\\\\\nF\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)&=\\frac{\\pi}{9}=\\frac{\\pi}{9}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(- \\frac{2}{9}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{9}\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\frac{\\pi}{9} - \\frac{2}{9}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694040 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12019bb2-d918-52a1-95c3-e42fd160a1fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694023}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694023} :answer-field/id #uuid "defce1ab-2273-5db1-9cd7-8ea709917a8b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ca39675d-730b-5c00-8b6e-0a1fa354e304" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\pi} - 2 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=- 2 x, & u^\\prime&=-2,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}, & v&=- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\pi}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\left(- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\left(-2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\pi}-\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{\\pi}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(\\pi\\right)&=\\pi=\\pi,\\\\\nF\\left(0\\right)&=0=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(\\pi\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=\\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694056 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "235b0043-f42f-517c-b76c-0c6c5957735b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694053} {:answer/id #uuid "41ecaa1d-f654-59d8-b849-303d53533faa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694058} {:answer/id #uuid "4dd3f94a-d93b-54ba-aac8-7c1ad4eed67c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694060} {:answer/id #uuid "52220479-eb3e-51eb-92dc-ca5be80a0098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694062} {:answer/id #uuid "6c0f9b08-70f4-51fb-b872-dbdbefe770b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694063}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694053} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a29a93-96da-527c-b7ef-e9f4430f4c9f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "30c5211d-64de-5dea-aef8-9c40edc08734" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} - 3 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=- 3 x, & u^\\prime&=-3,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}, & v&=- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[\\frac{3 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left(- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\left(-3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac{3 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}-\\frac{3}{2}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[\\frac{3 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2} - \\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)&=- \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}=- \\frac{3 \\pi}{4},\\\\\nF\\left(0\\right)&=0=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(- \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00efb0ca-1dce-55b8-afef-dc0d016dd030" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694047} {:answer/id #uuid "0dfb4527-b8d2-57bc-994b-9ebf97f12e24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694049} {:answer/id #uuid "190f64f7-7f7d-5ae7-aa24-d44dd643c58f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 - 2 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694052} {:answer/id #uuid "270c0972-6ba8-504b-889a-d58f0811613a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694054} {:answer/id #uuid "2f2cbf97-ea38-5b43-a574-4eaf41be65b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694055}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694055} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea1ea78d-8e6b-511e-a127-01e415908b71" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7eeff7ef-e0fa-52fb-8985-3cae13e42200" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{1} 2 x e^{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=2 x, & u^\\prime&=2,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=e^{x}, & v&=e^{x}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[2 x e^{x}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\left(2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[2 x e^{x}\\right]_{0}^{1}-2\\int_{0}^{1}e^{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[2 x e^{x} - 2 e^{x}\\right]_{0}^{1}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(1\\right)&=0=0,\\\\\nF\\left(0\\right)&=-2=-2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(0\\right)-\\left(-2\\right)\\\\\n&=2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694070 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43297437-d7d1-520e-991a-daaa8aed6a6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694059} {:answer/id #uuid "701599cf-42b3-5cca-b9ff-f32190ad0573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694064} {:answer/id #uuid "79513167-e7ba-5790-a094-9c7c4a610fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694065} {:answer/id #uuid "c3a95d6e-7c4f-5528-a701-46e6cb27110f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694069} {:answer/id #uuid "f22bc8b5-cf12-5fa7-9193-e45fe6983d09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694073}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694073} :answer-field/id #uuid "97dd1b57-605c-54c4-b620-392d5a8b788c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d71334ef-bb56-5c8c-b77d-0de5c15f6340" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=x, & u^\\prime&=1,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}, & v&=- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[- \\frac{x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\left(- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\left(1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[- \\frac{x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}+\\frac{1}{2}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[- \\frac{x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)&=\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4},\\\\\nF\\left(0\\right)&=0=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8c5de3-5466-5482-bbb1-bfc516c61d75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-9 + \\frac{9 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694048} {:answer/id #uuid "183e28c1-316f-5abe-99b9-73f73aa35644" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1 + \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694051} {:answer/id #uuid "3936598d-797e-58ac-a315-10942d5c16f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3 + \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694057} {:answer/id #uuid "51b5db63-5b56-50dc-8bf5-2b051f7e4c4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694061} {:answer/id #uuid "be4eac92-5be5-5f74-9305-0615280fb740" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3 + \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694068}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694057} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e2d7169-ab45-5f99-9bc0-8535a3d80a76" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "eb51afa4-db57-5d77-b316-24b39a993b42" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 3 x \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=3 x, & u^\\prime&=3,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}, & v&=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[3 x \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\left(3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[3 x \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}-3\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[3 x \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)&=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2},\\\\\nF\\left(0\\right)&=3=3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\right)-\\left(3\\right)\\\\\n&=-3 + \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694075 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec93b674-5708-5ba5-a9da-096cdee94dc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(- e^{3} - 2\\right)}{9 e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694084}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694084} :answer-field/id #uuid "69b07cc1-d4d1-56be-a289-65a62cbfeebf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "157482c6-c746-512b-ad51-044642c935a8" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{1}{3}}^{\\frac{2}{3}} - 2 x e^{3 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=- 2 x, & u^\\prime&=-2,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=e^{3 x}, & v&=\\frac{e^{3 x}}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[- \\frac{2 x e^{3 x}}{3}\\right]_{- \\frac{1}{3}}^{\\frac{2}{3}}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{- \\frac{1}{3}}^{\\frac{2}{3}}\\left(\\frac{e^{3 x}}{3}\\right)\\left(-2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[- \\frac{2 x e^{3 x}}{3}\\right]_{- \\frac{1}{3}}^{\\frac{2}{3}}+\\frac{2}{3}\\int_{- \\frac{1}{3}}^{\\frac{2}{3}}e^{3 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[- \\frac{2 x e^{3 x}}{3} + \\frac{2 e^{3 x}}{9}\\right]_{- \\frac{1}{3}}^{\\frac{2}{3}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)&=- \\frac{2 e^{2}}{9}=- \\frac{2 e^{2}}{9},\\\\\nF\\left(- \\frac{1}{3}\\right)&=\\frac{4}{9 e}=\\frac{4}{9 e}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(- \\frac{2 e^{2}}{9}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{4}{9 e}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{2 \\left(- e^{3} - 2\\right)}{9 e}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694077 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe72857b-13d7-5f5d-88ab-b100b6afbb27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\left(3 - 2 e\\right)}{4 e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694086}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694086} :answer-field/id #uuid "d91ca1fc-3b35-5190-b7fb-c408a1aaf188" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "42d4bb21-fc11-563a-a46b-8f8eb4ec74b7" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^{- \\frac{1}{2}} 3 x e^{2 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=3 x, & u^\\prime&=3,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=e^{2 x}, & v&=\\frac{e^{2 x}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[\\frac{3 x e^{2 x}}{2}\\right]_{-1}^{- \\frac{1}{2}}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{-1}^{- \\frac{1}{2}}\\left(\\frac{e^{2 x}}{2}\\right)\\left(3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac{3 x e^{2 x}}{2}\\right]_{-1}^{- \\frac{1}{2}}-\\frac{3}{2}\\int_{-1}^{- \\frac{1}{2}}e^{2 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[\\frac{3 x e^{2 x}}{2} - \\frac{3 e^{2 x}}{4}\\right]_{-1}^{- \\frac{1}{2}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)&=- \\frac{3}{2 e}=- \\frac{3}{2 e},\\\\\nF\\left(-1\\right)&=- \\frac{9}{4 e^{2}}=- \\frac{9}{4 e^{2}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(- \\frac{3}{2 e}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{9}{4 e^{2}}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{3 \\left(3 - 2 e\\right)}{4 e^{2}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694080 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3b81975-594c-5578-9ab2-0efdbc7d3db3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{8} - \\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694085}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694085} :answer-field/id #uuid "72655d85-0093-51a8-a7d9-4abd38c6442d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a4f3961b-db4e-5a9a-afaa-64fad4744f61" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} - 3 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=- 3 x, & u^\\prime&=-3,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}, & v&=\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[- \\frac{3 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\left(\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\left(-3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[- \\frac{3 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}+\\frac{3}{2}\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[- \\frac{3 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2} - \\frac{3 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)&=- \\frac{3 \\pi}{8}=- \\frac{3 \\pi}{8},\\\\\nF\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)&=\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{3}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(- \\frac{3 \\pi}{8}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\frac{3 \\pi}{8} - \\frac{3}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e29f779-2e9f-519b-93e6-7aea32f5adc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{2 \\pi}{9} - \\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694076}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694076} :answer-field/id #uuid "da9bab99-3792-539b-8b54-b01f3bf9d9bc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b91f918c-a8e0-5467-87f8-2807c112eb5b" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} - 2 x \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=- 2 x, & u^\\prime&=-2,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=\\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}, & v&=- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[\\frac{2 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}\\left(- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}\\right)\\left(-2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac{2 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[\\frac{2 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3} - \\frac{2 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{9}\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)&=- \\frac{2}{9}=- \\frac{2}{9},\\\\\nF\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)&=\\frac{2 \\pi}{9}=\\frac{2 \\pi}{9}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(- \\frac{2}{9}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{2 \\pi}{9}\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\frac{2 \\pi}{9} - \\frac{2}{9}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694089 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24d0b42a-bcf4-51c6-ab54-7d619fcc4415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6 x e^{- x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694093} {:answer/id #uuid "703ccc68-e8bb-50fb-a709-7a06443daab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-12 x e^{- x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694103} {:answer/id #uuid "94a32af5-4019-5d4b-8c8a-eaf31851e7a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6 x e^{- x} - 6 e^{- x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694107} {:answer/id #uuid "9b7679ab-d43d-57be-b79e-6b6ee74770fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6 x e^{- x} + 6 e^{- x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694109} {:answer/id #uuid "fa03e39a-50ff-56c3-b9ea-68b9aff83c21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6 x e^{- x} - 6 e^{- x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694121}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694121} :answer-field/id #uuid "74250762-f401-5a87-8f36-2ce48593ca34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694104}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "14bea470-184c-5ecf-9f29-5ddeabc665f9" :question/problem "Calculate\n\n$$\n\\int 6 xe^{- x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 6 xe^{- x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =6 x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′} & =e^{- x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=- e^{- x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6 x\\cdot e^{- x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6 x\\cdot (- e^{- x})-\\int (- e^{- x})\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-6 xe^{- x}+6\\cdot \\int e^{- x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6 xe^{- x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-6 xe^{- x}+6\\cdot \\int e^{- x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-6 xe^{- x}-6\\cdot e^{- x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollecting the linear terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6 xe^{- x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =-6 x e^{- x} - 6 e^{- x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694090 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43f17e0b-6268-57e2-b958-be505667edba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{x}{\\ln{(3 )}} + \\frac{1}{\\ln{(3 )}^{2}}\\right)3^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694099} {:answer/id #uuid "6691ac63-0715-5aa8-beda-5e6f73f58a58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{x}{\\ln{(3 )}} - \\frac{1}{\\ln{(3 )}^{2}}\\right)3^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694102} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ec7872-591d-54b6-8518-d1e7ab3fe837" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{x}{\\ln{(3 )}^{2}} + \\frac{x}{\\ln{(3 )}}\\right)3^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694114} {:answer/id #uuid "c6dd5d6e-cc9c-5f8c-b55c-33653930fb6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{x}{\\ln{(3 )}}\\right)3^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694115} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f8a7cc-fe5a-541c-af1c-c1dae3c73035" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{x}{\\ln{(3 )}} - \\frac{1}{\\ln{(3 )}^{2}}\\right)3^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694117}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694102} :answer-field/id #uuid "a26a53b2-9ce2-5c2a-a9de-7dfb9416db7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694111}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "19e99f60-9da4-54ea-bd6c-9fe3cc030a8c" :question/problem "$$\n\\int x3^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x3^{x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′} & =3^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{3^{x}}{\\ln{(3 )}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot 3^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{3^{x}}{\\ln{(3 )}}-\\int \\frac{3^{x}}{\\ln{(3 )}}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x3^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3^{x} x}{\\ln{(3 )}}-\\int \\frac{3^{x}}{\\ln{(3 )}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\ln{(3 )}}\\cdot x3^{x}-\\frac{1}{\\ln{(3 )}^{2}}\\cdot 3^{x}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3^{x}}{\\ln{(3 )}}(x - \\frac{1}{\\ln{(3 )}})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollecting the linear terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x3^{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\left(\\frac{x}{\\ln{(3 )}} - \\frac{1}{\\ln{(3 )}^{2}}\\right)3^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694098 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "044388a4-3e6a-5dae-8a22-4f1aae63b2b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(x - \\frac{1}{\\ln{(4 )}^{2}}\\right)4^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694087} {:answer/id #uuid "23c13642-8ef2-550b-8d1d-2292d0a5a4c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{x}{\\ln{(4 )}} - \\frac{1}{\\ln{(4 )}}\\right)4^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694092} {:answer/id #uuid "63433243-33c0-5af7-b7e1-896d58cd0728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{x}{\\ln{(4 )}^{2}} + \\frac{x}{\\ln{(4 )}}\\right)4^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694101} {:answer/id #uuid "7441a536-69e3-5178-8dad-512064ab445e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{x}{\\ln{(4 )}} - \\frac{1}{\\ln{(4 )}^{2}}\\right)4^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694105} {:answer/id #uuid "ae18c487-3421-594f-bf4d-3580e7cef989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{x}{\\ln{(4 )}} + \\frac{1}{\\ln{(4 )}^{2}}\\right)4^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694113}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694105} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef30f411-d368-586e-9bca-4a07c7d9cdb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3e25002e-622d-5e60-afd0-bf72bc97b78c" :question/problem "Calculate\n\n$$\n\\int x4^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x4^{x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′} & =4^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{4^{x}}{\\ln{(4 )}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot 4^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{4^{x}}{\\ln{(4 )}}-\\int \\frac{4^{x}}{\\ln{(4 )}}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x4^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{4^{x} x}{\\ln{(4 )}}-\\int \\frac{4^{x}}{\\ln{(4 )}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\ln{(4 )}}\\cdot x4^{x}-\\frac{1}{\\ln{(4 )}^{2}}\\cdot 4^{x}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4^{x}}{\\ln{(4 )}}(x - \\frac{1}{\\ln{(4 )}})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollecting the linear terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x4^{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\left(\\frac{x}{\\ln{(4 )}} - \\frac{1}{\\ln{(4 )}^{2}}\\right)4^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694100 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b31ff11-665c-5ceb-aa09-ce6857664124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2 x e^{- x} - 2 e^{- x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694091} {:answer/id #uuid "3752c634-e59b-54c6-9538-3ad3b3ed2392" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 x e^{- x} - 2 e^{- x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694097} {:answer/id #uuid "a8a6ba83-9504-542b-a023-cda0fa56347c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2 x e^{- x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694112} {:answer/id #uuid "d261cf9c-e09f-59e6-9e91-b721a36cb709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4 x e^{- x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694116} {:answer/id #uuid "f259a477-16c0-57f8-bcdd-43ddb60d3a5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2 x e^{- x} + 2 e^{- x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694120}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694091} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ed3fe3c-e657-5f42-8de6-6525f516315c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5ed16799-2411-53c4-b1f0-f3981135fac1" :question/problem "Calculate the integral\n\n$$\n\\int 2 xe^{- x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 2 xe^{- x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =2 x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′} & =e^{- x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=- e^{- x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2 x\\cdot e^{- x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2 x\\cdot (- e^{- x})-\\int (- e^{- x})\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2 xe^{- x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-2 xe^{- x}+2\\cdot \\int e^{- x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2 xe^{- x}-2\\cdot e^{- x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollecting the linear terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2 xe^{- x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =-2 x e^{- x} - 2 e^{- x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694108 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12a9a3b8-f018-553e-8f83-06dbaa1d70f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{6 x e^{7 x - 4}}{7} - \\frac{6 e^{7 x - 4}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694088} {:answer/id #uuid "274f3fbf-d27f-50ab-9c65-0749eab77a4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{6 x e^{7 x - 4}}{7} - \\frac{36 e^{7 x - 4}}{49}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694094} {:answer/id #uuid "32beccaa-15e1-5fa9-b88f-aa9382ec8ddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{6 x e^{7 x - 4}}{7} + \\frac{6 e^{7 x - 4}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694096} {:answer/id #uuid "a008af24-7ddd-5827-914c-fd63d76d869c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{6 x e^{7 x - 4}}{7} + \\frac{6 e^{7 x - 4}}{49}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694110} {:answer/id #uuid "deb81a55-59e3-518e-8374-0057bfba1a84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{6 x e^{7 x - 4}}{7} - \\frac{6 e^{7 x - 4}}{49}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694118}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694118} :answer-field/id #uuid "2be87ee8-ca80-5505-95e9-3e74dd2a5fe9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694095}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "95e9ca22-58f3-5e64-8045-179bb6e51fff" :question/problem "$$\n\\int 6 xe^{7 x - 4}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 6 xe^{7 x - 4}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =6 x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′} & =e^{7 x - 4}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{e^{7 x - 4}}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6 x\\cdot e^{7 x - 4}\\,\\text{d}x & =6 x\\cdot \\frac{e^{7 x - 4}}{7}-\\int \\frac{e^{7 x - 4}}{7}\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6 xe^{7 x - 4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 6 xe^{7 x - 4}-\\frac{6}{7}\\cdot \\int e^{7 x - 4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 6 xe^{7 x - 4}-\\frac{6}{49}\\cdot e^{7 x - 4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollecting the linear terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6 xe^{7 x - 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\frac{6 x e^{7 x - 4}}{7} - \\frac{6 e^{7 x - 4}}{49}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694125 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88048e6a-2f70-5035-a493-7b95701c52d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{4 x e^{6 x}}{3} + \\frac{4 e^{6 x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694123} {:answer/id #uuid "b29dae9c-35ba-5e46-85ed-752de6431d61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x e^{6 x}}{3} + \\frac{2 e^{6 x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694124} {:answer/id #uuid "cb1d0419-dae4-5f8d-a936-85024d60a873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x e^{6 x}}{3} - \\frac{2 e^{6 x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694126} {:answer/id #uuid "d2fba22b-7740-50b8-ac40-90d9be311fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x e^{6 x}}{3} - \\frac{4 e^{6 x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694127} {:answer/id #uuid "edf1ad24-151a-5ed7-90dd-37805a6c88ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x e^{6 x}}{3} - \\frac{e^{6 x}}{36}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694129}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694126} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcc41504-9ae9-5c53-8698-b5f4f258019b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694128}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b7c08dd9-661c-5fb8-b272-6f01e9991cca" :question/problem "$$\n\\int 8 xe^{6 x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 8 xe^{6 x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =8 x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=8 \\\\ {v}^{′} & =e^{6 x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{e^{6 x}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 8 x\\cdot e^{6 x}\\,\\text{d}x & =8 x\\cdot \\frac{e^{6 x}}{6}-\\int \\frac{e^{6 x}}{6}\\cdot 8\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 8 xe^{6 x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 8 xe^{6 x}-\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\int e^{6 x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 8 xe^{6 x}-\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot e^{6 x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollecting the linear terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 8 xe^{6 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\frac{4 x e^{6 x}}{3} - \\frac{2 e^{6 x}}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698499 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "161efaa4-6fd0-53da-9c11-aeeb079f0241" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+z)\\sin y+\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698495} {:answer/id #uuid "63b2c51b-4f21-55ec-ad71-ac3ec9f732fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+z)\\cos y+\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698503} {:answer/id #uuid "a336efc5-7ecd-5c97-8358-ab6757a932b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+z)\\cos y-(y+z)\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698505} {:answer/id #uuid "e91174e6-6944-537b-8e5c-ad55f2345825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+z)\\cos y+2\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698511} {:answer/id #uuid "fabc2531-3123-5abc-a009-b3030bbc2321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+z)\\cos y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698514}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698503} :answer-field/id #uuid "233d94ee-af31-5f67-a74a-3c0c40709443" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4f001fc3-1ece-55d3-b468-098ed948154d" :question/problem "Find $g_y(x,y,z)$ for $g(x,y,z)=(x+z)\\sin y+(y+z)\\cos x.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiate with respect to $y$, holding $x$ and $z$ fixed. Thus $x+z$ and $\\cos x$ are constants, while $y+z$ has derivative $1$.\n\nUsing the sum and constant multiple rules,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ng_y(x,y,z)&=(x+z)\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(\\sin y)+\\cos x\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(y+z)\\\\\n&=(x+z)\\cos y+\\cos x(1+0)\\\\\n&=(x+z)\\cos y+\\cos x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698506 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "341e3786-33df-5891-8d1d-d22f6dc17abe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698497} {:answer/id #uuid "57ff5808-4022-5091-8bc8-ae9ea203c4cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698501} {:answer/id #uuid "6679e71f-697e-5e1b-a9db-defbf3422a51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698504} {:answer/id #uuid "bb74518e-0276-5567-9a50-880e54985615" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698507} {:answer/id #uuid "dcaaf9f7-25fe-5a5b-90f9-9b4c483c6b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698509}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698501} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f822099-5820-55df-b31e-bb77759f3e53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a87ec839-cad9-515d-b29b-91381158b553" :question/problem "For the function $h(x,y,z)=z\\sqrt{4x^2+y^2},$ evaluate $\\dfrac{\\partial h}{\\partial x}$ at the point $(-2,3,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiate with respect to $x$, holding $y$ and $z$ fixed. The factor $z$ stays constant, and the square root requires the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial h}{\\partial x}&=z\\cdot\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4x^2+y^2}}\\cdot\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(4x^2+y^2)\\\\\n&=\\frac{z}{2\\sqrt{4x^2+y^2}}(8x+0)\\\\\n&=\\frac{4xz}{\\sqrt{4x^2+y^2}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow substitute $x=-2$, $y=3$, and $z=-1$. The radicand is $25>0$, so this derivative is defined at the point.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left.\\frac{\\partial h}{\\partial x}\\right|_{(-2,3,-1)}&=\\frac{4(-2)(-1)}{\\sqrt{4(-2)^2+3^2}}\\\\\n&=\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{25}}\\\\\n&=\\frac{8}{5}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
